# Procfile.example — development process manifest for overmind/hivemind.
#
# Usage:
#   cp Procfile.example Procfile       # then: overmind start  (or: hivemind)
#   cp Procfile.example Procfile.dev   # then: overmind start -f Procfile.dev
#                                      #   (or: hivemind Procfile.dev)
#
# Prerequisites:
#   - Valkey/Redis listening on 127.0.0.1:6379. If it isn't already running as
#     a service, uncomment the `valkey` line below to let the process manager
#     own it.
#   - FAMILIA_ADMIN_PASSPHRASE must be set on the Ruby process. If it is unset,
#     the server boots fine in development but rejects every login with the
#     generic "Authentication failed" (the spec's deliberate
#     reject-all-when-unset behavior). Overmind and hivemind both load a
#     sibling `.env` file automatically, so the simplest setup is:
#
#       echo "FAMILIA_ADMIN_PASSPHRASE='correct horse battery staple'" >> .env
#
#     (The inner single quotes land in .env and keep a passphrase containing
#     spaces intact — dotenv parsers strip them from the value.)
#
#     Passphrases shorter than 16 characters (Passphrase::MIN_LENGTH) warn at
#     boot in development and refuse to boot in any other environment.
#
# Once both processes are up, open the Vite URL it prints (default
# http://localhost:5173/login/) and enter the passphrase. The login POST goes
# through Vite's /admin/api proxy to the Ruby server on :9292; if your backend
# runs on a different port, also set FAMILIA_ADMIN_BACKEND=http://127.0.0.1:XXXX
# in .env so the proxy targets it.
#
# Note: `pnpm dev` serves the SPA on Vite's own port and proxies /admin/api to
# the Ruby backend. To exercise the full served gateway flow — the Ruby gate
# redirecting an unauthenticated browser to /login, then back to the
# cookie-gated web root after login — skip Vite: run `pnpm build`, then open
# http://127.0.0.1:9292/ against the Ruby server alone. `pnpm build` emits the
# single SPA the backend serves at both /login and the web root.

# valkey: valkey-server --port 6379
backend: bundle exec rackup
web: pnpm dev
